==Wauja==

===Noun===
{{head|wau|noun}}

# [[tapir]], ''Tapirus terrestris'' or (in Portuguese) ''anta''

#: A large nocturnal herbivorous mammal, with a stout body and a prehensile snout. They are commonly sighted in and near rivers. Their large splayed toes leave deep impressions in soft earth that are immediately recognizable as tapir tracks. In Wauja stories, the tapir is typically cast as a comical, clumsy and oafish character.

